yosys: memory_bmux2rom numbers its ROMs within their module

proc_rom and memory_bmux2rom named each ROM they create, its
$memrd/$meminit cells and proc_rom's read-data wire with NEW_ID:
`$auto$proc_rom.cc:155:do_switch$12665`. The number is the design-wide
autoidx, so it depends on every object yosys created before it anywhere
in the design. The same module elaborated alone, or once per instance,
or after a module with ROMs of its own, gets differently named ROMs,
and a flow that synthesizes a module on its own and inside its design
gets different netlists and memory lists for it.

A ROM is now numbered within its module, in the order the pass creates
them there: `$auto$proc_rom$<n>` and `$auto$memory_bmux2rom$<n>`, the
first n whose name and derived names ($rdata, $rd, $init) are free in
the module. Nothing else's naming changes.

Upstream candidate for YosysHQ/yosys; not filed. Carried by bazel-orfs
as four patches, one file each (Bazel applies one file per patch):
yosys-0003..0006. Retires at the bump onto a BCR yosys that names ROMs
within their module.

--- a/passes/memory/memory_bmux2rom.cc
+++ b/passes/memory/memory_bmux2rom.cc
@@ -46,6 +46,18 @@ struct MemoryBmux2RomPass : public Pass {
 		extra_args(args, argidx, design);
 
 		for (auto module : design->selected_modules()) {
+			// A ROM is numbered within its module, not by the design-wide
+			// autoidx, so the same module gets the same names whatever else
+			// the design holds.
+			int next_rom = 0;
+			auto rom_id = [&]() {
+				while (true) {
+					std::string id = stringf("$auto$memory_bmux2rom$%d", next_rom++);
+					if (!module->count_id(id) && !module->count_id(id + "$rd") &&
+							!module->count_id(id + "$init"))
+						return id;
+				}
+			};
 			for (auto cell : module->selected_cells()) {
 				if (cell->type != ID($bmux))
 					continue;
@@ -60,7 +72,8 @@ struct MemoryBmux2RomPass : public Pass {
 					continue;
 
 				// Ok, let's do it.
-				Mem mem(module, NEW_ID, width, 0, 1 << abits);
+				std::string id = rom_id();
+				Mem mem(module, id, width, 0, 1 << abits);
 				mem.attributes = cell->attributes;
 
 				MemInit init;
@@ -78,6 +91,8 @@ struct MemoryBmux2RomPass : public Pass {
 				mem.rd_ports.push_back(std::move(rd));
 
 				mem.emit();
+				module->rename(mem.inits[0].cell, id + "$init");
+				module->rename(mem.rd_ports[0].cell, id + "$rd");
 				module->remove(cell);
 			}
 		}
